name: precision fermentation cultivation process variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "An information content entity representing a set of process variables that groups relevant setpoint and measured process variables and describes the environmental and physicochemical parameters under which cells are cultivated, as well as the operational parameters by which the bioreactor system operates to maintain cell cultivation conditions throughout the fermentation process." []
synonym: "cultivation condition" RELATED []
synonym: "cultivation process variable" EXACT []
synonym: "cultivation variable" BROAD []
xref: EDAM:3724
is_a: PREFER:0000098 ! precision fermentation process variable
relationship: BFO:0000051 PREFER:9000000 ! has part precision fermentation setpoint process variable
relationship: BFO:0000051 PREFER:9000001 ! has part precision fermentation measured process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000009
name: feed setpoint process variable
def: "A precision fermentation setpoint process variable that defines the feed setpoint process variables of a bioreactor or fermentation system during the fermentation process." []
synonym: "precision fermentation feed setpoint process variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000037 ! feed medium cultivation process variable
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! precision fermentation setpoint process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000010
name: fermentation culture
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a cell population that is cultivated under controlled environmental conditions supporting a fermentation process." []
comment: Fermentation cultures are used in bioprocesses for various applications including precision fermentation, bioremediation, and production of biofuels and pharmaceuticals.
synonym: "cultured cell population" NARROW [OBI:0100060]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000010 PREFER:0000200 ! has fermentation culture type fermentation culture role

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000011
name: fermentation medium
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of an aqueous mixture of macronutrients, micronturients, and buffering agents that is used to support cell growth, metabolic activity and product formation during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "cultivation medium" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000004 CHEBI:24431 ! has medium ingredient chemical entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000012
name: cell biocatalyst
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a whole living cell that is used as a catalyst for bioproduction, catalyzing a biochemical reaction or transformation through their intrinsec or genetically modified metabolic activity." []
comment: In a biotransformation process or bioprocess, a cell biocatalyst converts substrates (organic or inorganic compounds) into outputs such as products, by-products, and cell biomass. Energy derived from substrate conversion is used for product formation, growth and cellular maintenance.
synonym: "biocatalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "biological catalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "catalyst" BROAD []
synonym: "cell catalyst" EXACT []
synonym: "cell factory" EXACT []
synonym: "microbial cell factory" NARROW []
synonym: "WCB" EXACT OMO:0003012 [DOI: 10.1201/9781003413134]
synonym: "whole-cell biocatalyst" EXACT [DOI: 10.1186/s12934-017-0724-7]
is_a: CL:0000000 ! cell
relationship: RO:0000086 PREFER:0000013 ! has quality taxon quality

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000013
name: taxon quality
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A quality of one or more biological organisms, as well as of parts of organism pertaining to a biological taxon." [PMID:18586729]
synonym: "taxon" BROAD [NCBITaxon:1]
xref: http://purl.org/biotop/btl2.owl#TaxonQuality
is_a: BFO:0000019 ! quality
relationship: RO:0000080 NCBITaxon:1 ! quality of root

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000014
name: bioreactor
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A device or system that is a material entity designed to support the run of a biological and biochemical process by controlling regulated environmental and cultivation conditions, such as temperature, agitation or nutrient injection at different scales, including lab-scale, pilot plant, and industrial-scale systems." [OBI:0001046]
comment: While this term is equivalent to OBI:0001046, PREFER has specific modelling that makes it more difficult to maintain if used directly. A decision was hence made to create this new term in PREFER and map it to OBI:0001046 instead.
synonym: "bioreactor system" EXACT []
synonym: "fermenter" NARROW [MSIO:0000167]
xref: OBI:0001046
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000185 ! has bioreactor scale bioreactor scale
relationship: PREFER:8000018 PREFER:0000180 ! has operational mode operation mode setpoint process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000015
name: obsolete operational parameter
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "OBSOLETE. An information content entity that represents a set of configurable settings used to operate and control a fermentation process, grouping setpoint process variables and mode dependent parameters that define how cultivation conditions are regulated in a bioreactor or fermentation system during the process." []
comment: The 'operational parameter' entity was deprecated because it was merged into 'Precision Fermentation Setpoint Process Variable', as all operational parameters were identified as setpoints.
synonym: "operational setting" BROAD []
synonym: "parameter" BROAD [NCIT:C44175]
xref: REPR:InstrumentSetting
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: PREFER:9000000

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000016
name: fermentation phase
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A time interval of a fermentation process." []
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process
relationship: BFO:0000050 PREFER:0000004 ! part of fermentation run

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000017
name: phase event
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "An operational intervention set by user that triggers the start or end of the fermentation phase." []
is_a: PREFER:9000003 ! precision fermentation process

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000018
name: offline sample
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A material entity consisting of a sample that has been withdrawn from a bioprocess system or bioreactor at a specific time point during the ongoing fermentation run for subsequent offline analysis of various compounds, such as substrates, products, and by-products, and biomass." []
synonym: "collected sample" EXACT []
synonym: "material sample" BROAD [OBI:0000747]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000019
name: temperature setpoint process variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation setpoint process variable that represents the target temperature value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "precision fermentation temperature setpoint process variable" EXACT []
synonym: "target temperature" EXACT []
synonym: "target temperature value" EXACT []
synonym: "target Tº" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature reference point" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature reference value" EXACT []
synonym: "temperature setting" EXACT [AFO_/result#AFR:0001255]
synonym: "Tº setpoint" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000007 ! temperature cultivation process variable
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! precision fermentation setpoint process variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 PREFER:9000004 ! has value specification unit
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000041 ! setpoint of temperature measured process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000020
name: pH setpoint process variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation setpoint process variable that represents the target pH value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "pH control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "ph control setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "ph setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "precision fermentation pH setpoint process variable" EXACT []
synonym: "target pH" EXACT []
synonym: "target ph" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000005 ! alkaline cultivation process variable
is_a: PREFER:9000000 ! precision fermentation setpoint process variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 uom:%5BpH%5D ! has value specification pH based unit
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000040 ! setpoint of pH measured process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000021
name: pH base solution
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A liquid material entity with basic (alkaline) properties that is used to increase the pH of a solution or system.\n\nIn a fermentation process, it is added manually or automatically to the fermentation run to control and maintain the pH at the defined setpoint or desired value." []
synonym: "pH control base solution" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000022
name: pH acid solution
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A liquid material entity with acidic properties that is used to decrease the pH of a solution or system.\n\nIn a fermentation process, it is added manually or automatically to the fermentation run to control and maintain the pH at the defined setpoint or desired value." []
synonym: "pH control acid solution" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000023
name: core balance metric
def: "A precision fermentation calculated process variable that represents a quantitative metric derived from balance calculations over a process, used to characterize the balance of inputs and outputs within a bioreactor or fermenter system during the fermentation process." []
synonym: "elemental balance metric" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:9000002 ! precision fermentation calculated process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000024
name: fermentation medium cultivation process variable
def: "A cultivation process variable that represents the fermentation medium related aspects of a fermentation cultivation process, grouping setpoint process variables and measured process variables that describe or regulate the state of the fermentation medium within the cultivation environment." []
is_a: PREFER:0000008 ! precision fermentation cultivation process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000025
name: target dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable that represents the target dissolved oxygen value to be regulated and maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "DO setpoint" EXACT OMO:0003012 []
synonym: "precision fermentation dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable" EXACT []
synonym: "target dissolved oxygen setpoint" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 uom:%25 ! has value specification percent
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000039 ! setpoint of dissolved oxygen measured process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000026
name: dissolved oxygen cascade level setpoint process variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable that represents the cascade control system linked to a parameter to achieve the desired dissolved oxygen level within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
comment: For instance, in fed-batch operation mode there could be three different cascade levels. Level 1 involves adjusting the stirrer speed parameter. Level 2 involves adjusting the air flow parameter. Level 3 involves adjusting the oxygen flow parameter.
synonym: "dissolved oxygen control strategy variable" EXACT []
synonym: "DO cascade level setpoint process variable" EXACT []
synonym: "precision fermentation dissolved oxygen cascade level setpoint process variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000027
name: maximum stirring setpoint process variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable that represents the target maximum revolutions per minute (rpm) of the bioreactor stirrer to be regulated and or maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "maximum shaking speed setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "maximum shaking speed setpoint process variable" EXACT []
synonym: "maximum stirring speed setpoint" EXACT []
synonym: "precision fermentation maximum stirring setpoint process variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000119 ! dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable
relationship: OBI:0001938 PREFER:7000008 ! has value specification revolution per minute
relationship: PREFER:8000020 PREFER:0000054 ! setpoint of stirrer speed measured process variable

[Term]
id: PREFER:0000028
name: minimum stirring setpoint process variable
namespace: precision_fermentation
def: "A precision fermentation dissolved oxygen setpoint process variable that represents the target minimum revolutions per minute (rpm) of the bioreactor stirrer to be regulated and or maintained within a bioreactor or fermentation system during a fermentation process." []
synonym: "minimum shaking speed setpoin" EXACT []
synonym: "minimum shaking speed setpoint process variable" EXACT []
synonym: "minimum stirring speed setpoin" EXACT []
synonym: "minimum stirring speed setpoint process variable" EXACT []
