[Term]
id: PREFER:0000070
name: BioLector XT - Beckman Coulter bioreactor
def: "A microbioreactor-scale high-throughput bioreactor system produced by Beckman Coulter Life Sciences for parallel cultivation of microbial or cell cultures simultaneously in up to 48-well microtiter plates (MTPs), each with a culture volume in the microliter range. It provides online optical monitoring of biomass, fluorescence, pH, and dissolved oxygen (DO) under orbital shaking conditions, using integrated pre-calibrated sensor technology and optional microfluidic modules for automated feeding and pH control." [https://www.mybeckman.dk/microbioreactor/biolector-xt]
