[Term]
id: PREFER:8000049
name: Biofoundry
def: "An organisation that is an integrated molecular biology facility that includes robotic liquid-handling equipment, high-throughput analytical equipment, and the software, personnel and data management systems required to run the equipment and broader biofoundry capabilities." [PMID:33817343]
is_a: OBI:0000245 ! organization

[Term]
id: PREFER:8000053
name: Growth Profiler 960 - Enzyscreen bioreactor
def: "A microbioreactor-scale bioreactor produced by Enzyscreen that cultivates and optically monitors up to 960 microbial or cell cultures simultaneously in ten 96-square-well microtiter plates (MTPs), each with a culture volume of 0.25 mL. the system combines orbital shaking incubation with time-resolved bottom imaging and automated image-based biomass quantification." [https://www.enzyscreen.com/article/How-does-it-work/]
is_a: PREFER:0000014 ! bioreactor
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000085 ! has bioreactor scale micro bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:8000054
name: TOM - Kuhner bioreactor
def: "A bench-scale shaken bioreactor online monitoring system produced by Kuhner that enables parallel monitoring of up to 16 individual shake flasks. The system measures oxygen transfer rate (OTR), carbon dioxide transfer rate (CTR), and respiratory quotient (RQ) through automated analysis of respiratory gas exchange during orbital shaking incubation." [https://kuhner.com/wAssets/docs/download/Maschinendokumentation/Information-Flyer-KuhnerTOM-en-_2025.pdf]
comment: This system is classified under bioreactor because of its use in conjunction with biological cultivation workflows. However, the Kuhner TOM is not strictly a bioreactor. Rather, it is an online respiratory gas monitoring and analytical system that measures oxygen transfer rate (OTR), carbon dioxide transfer rate (CTR), and respiratory quotient (RQ) in cultures grown in orbitally shaken vessels such as shake flasks.
is_a: PREFER:0000014 ! bioreactor
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000186 ! has bioreactor scale bench bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:8000055
name: Livit Flex - Getinge bioreactor
def: "A bench-scale bioreactor bioprocess control system produced by Getinge that monitors and regulates cultivation parameters in connected single-use or reusable bioreactors through integrated control software, sensor interfaces, fluid handling components, and gas management functions. It can be configured as single or dual control system with vessel total volumes ranging from 2 to 20 L." [https://www.getinge.com/int/products/livit-flex/]
comment: Former manufacturer is Applikon Biotechnology
is_a: PREFER:0000014 ! bioreactor
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000186 ! has bioreactor scale bench bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:8000056
name: BioBench - Biostream bioreactor
def: "A bench-scale stirred-tank bioreactor produced by Biostream with a working volume of approximately 5 liters, integrated with the Lucullus process information management platform for automated monitoring, control, and data acquisition during biological cultivation processes." [https://www.biostream-international.com/biobench/]
is_a: PREFER:0000014 ! bioreactor
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000186 ! has bioreactor scale bench bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:8000057
name: Biostat Cplus - Sartorius bioreactor
def: "A pilot-scale stirred-tank bioreactor produced by Sartorius with a working volume of approximately 30 liters, integrated with the Lucullus process information management platform for automated monitoring, control, and data acquisition during biological cultivation processes." [https://www.sartorius.com/en/products/fermentation-bioreactors/stainless-steel-bioreactors/biostat-cplus]
is_a: PREFER:0000014 ! bioreactor
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000187 ! has bioreactor scale pilot bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:8000058
name: Proreact P15 - Frings bioreactor
def: "A pilot-scale stirred-tank bioreactor produced by Frings with a working volume of approximately 100 liters, integrated with the Lucullus process information management platform for automated monitoring, control, and data acquisition during biological cultivation processes. The system is intended for research, process development, and scale-up studies and is designed with automation and operational concepts comparable to industrial production processes." [https://frings.com/en/produkte/proreact-p-production-bioreactors/]
is_a: PREFER:0000014 ! bioreactor
relationship: PREFER:8000008 PREFER:0000187 ! has bioreactor scale pilot bioreactor scale

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000000
name: precision fermentation setpoint process variable
def: "An information content entity that represents a collection of configurable control settings for a fermentation system, which is realized as configuration input used to regulate a fermentation process by specifying operational setpoints, controller parameters, target values, and other mode-dependent control parameters in a bioreactor or fermentation system during the process." []
comment: A decision was made to classify this as a information content entity rather than realizable entity (a realizable entity that inheres in a system and is realized in processes of controlling or regulating a process, serving as a parameter or setting that affects or determines the behavior, operation, or outcome of that process) as the intention was to emphasize the informational role rather than physical realisation of the control.\n\nA setpoint process variable may vary depending on the selected fermentation operational mode (e.g. batch, fed-batch, continuous) and are realized through instrument or system configuration.
synonym: "operational parameter" BROAD []
synonym: "operational setting" BROAD []
synonym: "parameter" BROAD [NCIT:C44175]
xref: REPR:InstrumentSetting
is_a: PREFER:0000098 ! precision fermentation process variable
property_value: dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000001
name: precision fermentation measured process variable
def: "A precision fermentation process variable that specifically represents measurable attributes or values that are the outcomes of a measurement process aimed at determining characteristics of said process." []
synonym: "measured process variable" BROAD []
xref: VO:0010241
is_a: PREFER:0000098 ! precision fermentation process variable
relationship: PREFER:8000059 OBI:0001508 ! measured at time datum sampling time measurement datum
property_value: dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000002
name: precision fermentation calculated process variable
def: "A precision fermentation process variable that is the output of a calculation or computation based on one or more measured or other input variables, representing derived or computed attributes related to the fermentation process." []
synonym: "calculated process variable" EXACT []
synonym: "computed process variable" EXACT []
is_a: PREFER:0000098 ! precision fermentation process variable
property_value: dc:contributor "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596" xsd:string

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000003
name: precision fermentation process
def: "A process that involves precision fermentation." []
comment: Precision fermentation is a biotechnological method used in industrial or research settings that employs genetically engineered or adaptatively laboratory-evolved (ALE) microorganisms (such as bacteria, yeast, fungi or microalgae) to produce specific, high-value compounds with precise molecular structures. This process involves controlled environments—such as operating bioreactor parameters(e.g., temperature, pH, dissolved oxygen, agitation, nutrient feed) and upstream preparation conditions(e.g., pre-culture growth, strain storage, and defined media composition)—where microbial metabolism is optimized to synthesize target products, such as proteins, enzymes, or bioactive molecules, often with greater efficiency, yield, and specificity than traditional fermentation methods.
is_a: COB:0000082 ! planned process
relationship: BFO:0000051 GO:0006113 ! has part fermentation

[Term]
id: PREFER:9000004
name: unit
def: "An information content entity that represents a standard quantity or measurement used to express the magnitude of a quantity." []
comment: The decision to utilise https://units-of-measurement.org/ meant that we did not want to commit to any unit ontologies. We hence created our own parent class to parent units. Interoperability of units can be achieved by the matches in units-of-measurement, and this term should only be used to constraining in modelling.
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

